    "record_text_excerpt": "Near-Yrast spectroscopy of <sup>164</sup>Yb and neighbouring nuclei : Systematics of octupole bands and bandcrossings | Lund University Publications Skip to main content LUND UNIVERSITY | LUND UNIVERSITY LIBRARIES search all top articles Lund University Publications LUND UNIVERSITY LIBRARIES Register publications | Statistics | Marked list 0 | Saved searches 0 Advanced Home Publications Departments Near-Yrast spectroscopy of 164 Yb and neighbouring nuclei : Systematics of octupole bands and bandcrossings Mark Jónsson, S. ; Roy, N. ; Ryde, H. LU ; Waluś, W. ; Kownacki, J. ; Garrett, J. D. ; Hagemann, G. B. ; Herskind, B. ; Bengtsson, R. LU and Åberg, S. LU ( 1986 )\n\n\n        In Nuclear Physics, Section A 449 (3) . p.537-578 Abstract High-spin states in 164 Yb have been populated in the 152 Sm( 16 O, 4n) and 150 Sm( 18 O, 4n) reactions. From studies of γγ coincidences, γ-ray angular distributions and conversion electron measurements the level scheme has been constructed. The g-band and the S-band have been established to spin and parity 22 + and 26 +' , respectively, and the rotational sequences (π, α) = (-, 1) 1 , (-, 0) 1 and (-, 0) 2 to 23 - , 24 - and 18 - , respectively. Constructed two-quasineutron configurations and cranked shell model calculations are compared with the experimental results. Residual interactions between quasiparticles... (More) High-spin states in 164 Yb have been populated in the 152 Sm( 16 O, 4n) and 150 Sm( 18 O, 4n) reactions. From studies of γγ coi"
